1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,007
The TDP on your CPU box is not how much power it uses.

2
00:00:05,287 --> 00:00:06,527
It's a cooling number.

3
00:00:07,277 --> 00:00:10,014
TDP means thermal design power.

4
00:00:10,294 --> 00:00:14,217
It tells cooler makers how much heat to plan for at base speed.

5
00:00:14,497 --> 00:00:16,103
Boost is another story.

6
00:00:16,853 --> 00:00:18,992
So Intel now lists two figures.

7
00:00:19,272 --> 00:00:29,739
The Core i9-14900K has a base power of 125 watts, but a max turbo power of 253 watts.

8
00:00:30,019 --> 00:00:31,007
More than double.

9
00:00:31,757 --> 00:00:33,003
AMD is similar.

10
00:00:33,283 --> 00:00:39,114
The Ryzen 7 7700X is rated at 105 watts TDP.

11
00:00:39,394 --> 00:00:43,966
Its power limit, called PPT, is 142 watts.

12
00:00:44,716 --> 00:00:50,871
So size your cooler and power supply on the turbo or PPT figure, not the small one.

13
00:00:51,621 --> 00:00:54,187
More PC hardware explained on the channel.

